# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env to version control.
#
# Every variable the tree reads stands here, and nothing else does: a documented
# variable no code reads is a lie. A test that diffs this file against the
# os.environ / ${NAME} readers keeps both directions true.
#
# Used by: docker-compose.prod.yml as shipped (docker-compose.yml's postgres service and the Makefile's include .env are commented out until enabled)

# ── Compose (server only) ──
# Lets plain `docker compose` and scripts/backup-postgres.sh target the prod stack.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.prod.yml
# Must equal PROJECT in the Makefile (default myapp), or it targets another stack.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=myapp

# ── Database ──
POSTGRES_USER=admin
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<your-db-password>
POSTGRES_DB=<your-database-name>

# ── Application ──
# APP_PORT=8080
# APP_ENV=production

# ── Secrets ──
# JWT_SECRET=<your-jwt-secret>

# ── Monitoring ──
# Dead-man's-switch URLs (e.g. Better Stack heartbeats), pinged only on success.
# Setup: guides/monitoring.md.
# Pinged by scripts/backup-postgres.sh after a verified backup:
# BACKUP_PING_URL=<your-ping-url>
# Pinged by the certbot service after a successful `certbot renew`:
# CERT_PING_URL=<your-ping-url>
